The function `wl1271_tx_allocate()` returns `-EAGAIN` when `pskb_expand_head()` fails due to insufficient memory. The caller `wlcore_tx_work_locked()` interprets `-EAGAIN` as the aggregation buffer being full, leading to an infinite retry loop and CPU soft lockup.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
