    pskb_expand_head(skb, (total_len - skb->len), 0, GFP_ATOMIC)) {
    wl1271_free_tx_id(wl, id);
    return -ENOMEM;
}
```
Reason:
Changing the return value from `-EAGAIN` to `-ENOMEM` ensures the caller treats the failure as an out‑of‑memory condition rather than an aggregation buffer full condition, so it drops the packet and terminates the retry loop instead of attempting infinite retries.

